# The services and one-shots init starts for the app host (docs/app-host.md,
# `guest-init --only`): what an app's start needs without system_server.
# apexd, keystore2 and odsign set properties init waits for; SurfaceFlinger
# waits for the power HAL at its first frame; vold mounts the emulated
# storage the agent serves; audioserver plays apps' sound, and takes wake
# locks of system_suspend; the media services decode and play what apps'
# players and the sound effects play; cameraserver serves apps the Mac's
# cameras through the camera provider; the health HAL reports the Mac's
# battery to the battery service; netd hosts DnsResolver, which resolves
# apps' names on the network the connectivity service gives it, once
# bpfloader has marked the BPF programs loaded; statsd takes the atoms apps
# log and serves the stats manager's calls; the Bluetooth HAL is the
# controller the Bluetooth app's stack drives over the Mac's CoreBluetooth;
# aim-appsearch runs the original AppSearch module, which only system_server
# would run; tombstoned keeps the tombstones crash_dump writes and the stack
# traces processes dump on SIGQUIT; installd creates apps' data directories
# as the package side asks (`createAppData`).
